n Colorado...\nSoutheastern Sedgwick County in northeastern Colorado...\nNortheastern Washington County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 930 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 725 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 0.5 and 1.5 inches of rain\nhave fallen.\n\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are expected over the\narea. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nHolyoke, Haxtun, Otis, Paoli, Highland Center, Fairfield, Lone\nStar, Sixteen-Mile Corner, Amherst, Burdett, Pleasant Valley,\nPlatner and Hyde.","ends":"2026-08-15T21:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Logan, CO; Phillips, CO; Sedgwick, CO; Washington, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b5fc3fb0f4468acf2c3b7dde0584271abf13df82.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b5fc3fb0f4468acf2c3b7dde0584271abf13df82.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 15 at 7:17PM MDT until August 15 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of east central and northeast Colorado, including\neastern Elbert, Lincoln, Washington, Sedgwick, and Phillips\nCounties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Additional thunderstorms and heavy rainfall this evening,\ncombined with the heavy rainfall from the past 3 days, will bring\na threat for flash flooding this afternoon and evening. Stronger\nstorms will be capable of producing 1 to 2 inches of rain in 30\nminutes, with isolate